WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.725
The Cannabis compute client uses a general-purpose workload contract. Package your

00:00:04.725 --> 00:00:09.450
software, declare its runtime, specify inputs and outputs, and set resource

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:09.880
limits.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.946
New adapters can extend the format. A script, a virtual machine

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:17.732
checkpoint, a renderer, or coordinated model training can each describe what

00:00:17.732 --> 00:00:18.420
they need.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.631
Whole jobs can target one suitable node. Workloads with declared dependencies

00:00:22.631 --> 00:00:26.522
can form a task graph. Distributed programs can request compatible groups.

00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:30.413
The runtime and splitting rules preserve what your program is meant

00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:31.120
to do.
